message: Please cite this dataset when using its transcription or documentation. CC-BY-4.0 identifies original documentation; historical text and excluded source images have separate statuses in RIGHTS.md.
type: dataset
title: '皮膚新編（1874；Bodleian Sinica 1790）：轉錄與中英醫名對照 / Pi fu xin bian [Manual of skin diseases]: Transcription and bilingual terminology'
version: 0.2.0
authors:
- family-names: Chu
  given-names: Chen-Yu
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-9738-6914
url: https://github.com/poplolioi11/bodleian-sinica1790-pifu-xinbian-1874
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: Pi fu xin bian [Manual of skin diseases] was orally translated by John Glasgow Kerr and written down by Lin Xiangdong, and published by the Boji medical institution in Canton in 1874; this copy is Bodleian Sinica 1790. Its English notice identifies the latter part of Fenwick’s Medical Diagnosis as its basis and describes Canton names, transliteration and terminology collection. The work contains 128 sections in eight internal divisions, appended formulas, figure labels and bilingual names. Version 0.2.0 combines a fixed initial transcription of 117 original-print faces with a separately sealed independent AI reading, followed by full-face nonblind source-image adjudication. JSON, TXT and TEI retain source strings; table cells, original blanks and ditto marks, note anchors and uncertainty records support histories of medicine, translation and medical missions. Source images are excluded. No full human double collation, expert approval or accuracy measurement is claimed.
